      "concern": "Headless CLI execution is not pinned or provenance-checked; commands appear to be invoked as bare `claude`, `codex`, and `gemini` from the ambient PATH.",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "severity_score": 880,
      "why_matters": "A PATH-hijacked or compromised CLI can exfiltrate OAuth/session credentials, prompts, model outputs, and audit metadata. Redaction protects logs after capture, but does not protect against a malicious executable or unexpected CLI version behavior.",
      "location": "Sprint 2 T2.0, T2.9, T2.12; FR-4 doctor; headless dispatch subprocess call sites",
      "recommendation": "Resolve CLIs via configured absolute paths, validate ownership/permissions, capture and enforce allowed version ranges, optionally verify checksums/signatures where feasible, and fail closed with `[CONFIG-INVALID]` if binary provenance checks fail.",
