      "why_matters": "The cycle thesis depends on headless CLI reliability under load, but default mocked stress tests can pass while live CLIs fail due to hidden session locks, browser-profile contention, provider limits, or local credential-store behavior.",
      "location": "Sprint 2 AC2.10, T2.16; Sprint 3 rollout gate; G-4 empirical window",
      "recommendation": "Make a bounded live concurrency verification mandatory before Sprint 3 for each provider, even if at low N, with operator-approved safeguards. Use mocked tests for CI but require live attestation artifacts for rollout readiness.",
