      "concern": "Symlink and tempfile handling in `.run` is risky without explicit directory ownership, permissions, and race protections.",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "severity_score": 735,
      "why_matters": "The plan creates transitional symlinks and a startup janitor that scans `.run/tmp-redaction-*`. If `.run` is writable by other users or subject to symlink/race manipulation, cleanup or migration logic can be abused for denial of service, state spoofing, or unsafe file operations.",
      "location": "Sprint 1 D1.3, D1.6, T1.3, T1.4; Carry-ins C8 and C13",
      "recommendation": "Require `.run` to be mode 0700 or otherwise owner-restricted, use `openat`/`unlinkat`-style safe path handling where possible, never follow symlinks for janitor targets, validate file ownership before deletion, and add tests for hostile symlinks and TOCTOU races.",
      "source": "tertiary_skeptic"
